"Chaos Master" <erana.ovepx@ibestvip.com.br> wrote:

> - There is a list of messages in engrave.c, as in:

> static const char *epitaphs[] = {
>         "Rest in peace",
>         "R.I.P.",
>       ...
> };

> Can I just add my message to the list?

Even though you already know that it works, you might want
to know why.

In the same file, the line:

  if (!str) str = epitaphs[rn2(SIZE(epitaphs))];

occurs, which is asking how long the list is, before casting
a random number to choose one string from the list. Thus you
can indeed just add new messages to the list without making
changes elsewhere; the software adjusts itself automatically
to your additions.

[At least in the 3.4.2 source, the last one I've bothered to
download, that list as it exists does not have a comma (",")
after the last string. The C language allows such a trailing
comma, and over the years, accepted good coding practice has
been to include one, so you might want to do that while
you're changing the list anyway.]

